      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $B?$\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 & 4 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -7 & 4 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
